Subject: [PATCH] Restore the fork test cases the merge resolved away
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five suites came out of the merge holding upstream's version of a file the fork
had also extended, so the cases guarding fork behaviour went with it: the
collapsed action bar, the sender and order filters on search, the search header
and its match stepper, the jump-to-date affordance and the header search
button. Every one of them still guards live source on this branch, so the
behaviour shipped untested rather than unshipped.

Each suite is extended in place rather than replaced with the feature branch's
copy. Taking the branch's file wholesale reads as an improvement — the test
count goes up — while silently deleting the cases other branches had added to
the same file since.

One case does not pass yet and is left failing rather than hidden: with the
search-header suite present, "should leave the caret in the search box when it
is emptied" loses the caret to a button. It passes alone and fails after that
suite runs, so two branches' tests are sharing state through something neither
resets.
